# Read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages from dist/.
# The first fastconfirm.it linked four one-pager PDFs; partners may still have those links.
# Each now points at the docs page that replaced it.
/FCR_Interop_One_Pager.pdf                         /docs/integrate/bridges        301
/Fast%20Confirmation%20Rule%20for%20Exchanges.pdf  /docs/integrate/exchanges      301
/Fast%20Confirmation%20Rule%20for%20L2s.pdf        /docs/integrate/rollups        301
/Fast%20Confirmation%20Rule%20for%20RPCs.pdf       /docs/integrate/rpc-providers  301

# Unknown URLs get a not-found page with a 404 status: the docs' own under /docs/, the site's everywhere
# else (the docs' page outside /docs/ broke: its router jumped to /docs/ and showed an empty page).
# Netlify only finds a root 404.html on its own, so the docs need their rule. Rules without ! never
# shadow files that exist, so real pages are unaffected. Keep these last.
/docs/*  /docs/404.html  404
/*       /404.html       404
